Risk-Based Approach to Role-Based Training for
KYC Analyst (Enhanced Due Diligence / EDD)
For illustrative purpose
This role does not own the customer relationship and does not make commercial decisions. The responsibility is risk understan ding and escalation.
1
Role Function / The why?
The KYC Analyst (EDD) conducts enhanced due diligence on high-risk
customers to ensure that the bank has a complete and sound
understanding of the customer's identity, business, source of funds, and
the actual risk associated with the customer.
The role is a critical control function that shall prevent the bank from
establishing or maintaining customer relationships linked to money
laundering, terrorist financing, or other financial crime.

2 Main Areas of Responsibility
• Conduct enhanced due diligence (EDD) for higher-risk customers
• Review and validate customer ownership, control, and corporate/organisational
structure
• Assess source of funds and source of wealth where required
• Perform periodic KYC reviews based on risk level
• Identify discrepancies between customer information and observed behaviour
• Document risk assessments and conclusions in a manner that is auditable and
regulator-ready
• Escalate suspicious indicators to AML investigations as needed
3 Inherent AML Exposure
• Handles the bank's highest-risk customers
• Relies on professional judgement, not just checklists
• Weak or flawed analysis can allow illegitimate customers to go
undetected
• Failure to escalate can directly lead to regulatory breaches
4 Key Risk Themes
• Risk related to beneficial ownership and control
• Risk in high-risk customer onboarding
• Risk related to ongoing customer due diligence and periodic reviews
• Jurisdictional and geographic risk
• Risk related to documentation and audit trail
• Risk related to escalation and reporting

5. Regulatory Accountability — Key Obligations
• Apply a risk-based approach to customer due diligence
• Perform due diligence on high-risk customers
• Maintain accurate and up-to-date customer information
• Identify and escalate suspicious activity
• Maintain clear documentation and audit trail
6. Role-Specific Competence
Knowledge
• Enhanced due diligence
(EDD) requirements
• Ownership and control
structures
• Concepts of source of
funds and source of wealth
• AML typologies relevant to
the bank's customers
Skills
• Analyse complex customer
structures
• Assess the plausibility of
financial
explanations/narratives
• Write clear, well-reasoned risk
rationales
• Identify red flags and
inconsistencies/discrepancies
Judgement
• Knowing when explanations
are insufficient
• Escalating under
uncertainty
• Applying standards
consistently, even under
pressure

The Result → Role-specific, Risk-based Compliance Training
1.Training: guidelines, standards, risk-based approach, etc.
2. Training is updated annually
and when regulations,
typologies, or internal
findings change
3. Enhanced due diligence
(EDD) and case handling
Source of wealth and
source of funds
4. Structures for beneficial
owners (beneficial
