How to build a
compliance training
program:
Example training plans tailored to roles

Training plan: Transaction Monitoring Analyst
This training plan is built around the specific risks, regulations, and behaviours required for the Transaction Monitoring
Analyst role. It is designed not just to build knowledge, but to drive genuine behavioural change: ensuring regulatory
obligations are understood, internalised, and consistently applied in day-to-day work.
Q1 Q1
Q1: Foundation Q2: Application Q3: Deepening Q4: Embedding
Yearly Wheel
Q1
Q1
Training Philosophy
• Year 1 is intensive: building foundation, applying knowledge, and
assessing competency
• Years 2–4 maintain and deepen skills through annual refreshers, specialist
development, and peer contribution
• Behavioural change is evidenced through QA reviews, assessments, and
reflective practice
• Regulatory literacy is built progressively — not just ticked off once

