EU regulation (2024/1624) requiring function-specific, risk-based and documented AML training
Laws, regulations and procedures to prevent criminals from disguising illegal funds as legitimate income
Process of verifying client identity and assessing risk profile before and during a business relationship
Identifying and verifying a customer's identity and assessing the risk they pose — a core KYC obligation
Higher level of scrutiny applied to high-risk customers such as PEPs or those from high-risk jurisdictions
Individual holding a prominent public position, requiring enhanced scrutiny due to elevated corruption risk
Software platform used to assign, deliver, track and report on training and learning activities
Designated person in a regulated firm responsible for receiving and assessing suspicious activity reports
Senior executive overseeing the organisation's compliance programme and regulatory obligations
EU regulatory agency issuing guidelines and technical standards for the banking sector, including AML/CFT
Intergovernmental body setting global standards for combating money laundering and terrorist financing
EU regulation governing the collection, processing and storage of personal data
Process to identify and mitigate data privacy risks — required under GDPR for high-risk processing activities